I fixed `parseCSV` in `csv.js`, and `node test.js` now prints `OK`.

- **Empty input:** `""` now returns `[]` instead of `[[""]]`.
- **Trailing newline:** if the text ends with a newline, the empty last line is dropped, so there's no extra empty row.

Only one trailing newline is dropped. Input ending in `"\n\n"` still produces one empty row, which keeps blank lines that are actually part of the data. It also still splits only on `\n`, so files with Windows line endings (`\r\n`) will leave a `\r` at the end of the last field in each row.


